lake went from the  child star of mgm's little rascals to  the enigmatic mystery man in lost  highway unfortunately his role in the  mind-bending david lynch film wherein he  plays an entity who induces a man to  kill his wife would be his last before  the murder of his real-life wife in  2001. on may 4th 2001 bonnie lee bakely  was found shot dead in blake's car which  was parked around the corner from the  studio city restaurant the couple ate at  that night blake claimed that he had  returned to the restaurant to collect  his missing gun when the fatal shooting  of his wife took place although a police  investigation determined that blake's  missing gun was not the one used to kill  bakely blake was arrested in 2002 when  two former stuntmen came forward  claiming that the actor had tried to  hire them both to murder his wife on  separate occasions blake was eventually  acquitted three years later but a later  civil court claim later found him guilty  of intentionally causing bakeley's death  and ordered him to pay 30 million  dollars to bakeley's children blick's  criminal trial was the nail in his  career coffin but that didn't stop the  senior actor from issuing a plea to  producers in the aftermath he proclaimed  himself broke and announced that he was  available for work unsurprisingly work  never came  the 1980 season was a transitional one  for saturday night live with the  remainder of its original cast departing  in favor of a new group of comedians  including eddie murphy joe piscapo and  charles rocket producer gene domanium  apparently thought rocket would be her  breakout star an actor in comic in the  mold of snl alzheimer's bill murray and  chevy chase rocket indeed made a name  for himself on snl with the rocket  report a cheeky series of pre-taped man  on the street bits but it was a live  blunder that did him in in a parody of  the who shot jr craze on dallas a  reference to guest hosts and dallas  co-star charlene tilton an unknown  fictional assassin shot rocket in an  abrupt conclusion to the sketch at the  end of the episode with the entire cast  gathered on stage tilton asked rocket  how he was doing  charlie how are you feeling after you've  been shot oh man it's the first time  i've been shot in my life i'd like to  know  within weeks rocket was fired from snl  due to the language he used he went on  to have a modest movie career usually  playing yuppies jerks and dads and  things like earth girls are easy hocus  pocus and dumb and dumber but nothing  approaching the resumes of murray and  chase tragically rocket died by suicide  in 2005 at age 56.  a major star of the silent film era  roscoe fatty arbuckle was at the height  of his fame when hollywood's first major  scandal permanently derailed his life  and career on september 5th 1921 the  actor and comedian booked three rooms at  the saint francis hotel where he was  planning on throwing a party an aspiring  actress named virginia rapp was one of  several women who were extended in  invitation but her decision to accept  would prove to be a fatal one rap was  eventually found seriously ill in room  1219 the room arbuckle was sleeping in  after allegedly telling people arbuckle  had hurt her she died four days later of  a ruptured bladder arbuckle was arrested  and charged with manslaughter but the  jury failed to reach a verdict and a  mistrial was called after a second trial  yielded the same result arbuckle's legal  team stepped up their defense making  sure that the third one went in their  favor although the actor was eventually  acquitted it was too late his career was  over his films were banned and his  legacy was left in tatters  playing michaela baines in 2007's  transformers made megan fox an overnight  sensation  within a couple of years she'd return  for the sequel transformers revenge of  the fallen starred as the titular  jennifer in the cult [ __ ] comedy  jennifer's body and played a supporting  role in how to lose friends and alienate  people unfortunately for the rising star  she was about to lose some friends and  alienate plenty of people herself in  2009 fox sat down for an interview with  the uk magazine wonderland when asked a  softball question about working with  transformers director michael bay fox  answered honestly and provocatively  saying he's like napoleon and he wants  to create this insane infamous madman  reputation fox's historical comparisons  weren't done though as she continued he  wants to be like hitler on his sets and  he is despite the extremely unflattering  comparison base still wanted to rehire  fox for transformers dark of the moon  however he was reportedly overruled by  producer steven spielberg who directed  schindler's list and founded the  survivors of the showa visual history  foundation  fox's team denied reports that she'd  been ousted stating that she'd left the  project of her own volition but the  damage was done ever since fox has  appeared in a couple of teenage mutant  ninja turtle movies a few episodes of  new girl and a music video for her  fiance machine gun kelly  gilbert gottfried was something of a  minor pop culture icon in the 1980s and  early 1990s after a one-season stint on  saturday night live in the early 80s he  popped up in numerous comedy movies and  tv shows including beverly hills cop 2  the adventures of fort fairlane and the  problem child trilogy even if you didn't  know his face you definitely knew his  voice an abrasive grating rasp that  served him well as a voice actor  godfrey's most iconic voice roles were  both birds he played iago the parrot in  disney's aladdin and the aflac duck in a  series of iconic insurance commercials  off-screen gottfried made much of his  living as a relentlessly touring club  comedian it was in that mode where  gottfried issued some remarks that  ripped tremendous damage on his career  and reputation when a devastating  earthquake and tsunami hit japan in 2011  killing at least 3 000 people gottfried  was quick to tweet out a dozen dark  one-liners among them japan is really  advanced they don't go to the beach the  beach comes to them twitter users called  out gottfried for what they felt was bad  taste and questionable judgment while  the comedian's bosses at aflac gave him  the boot aflac cmo michael zuna told the  ap there is no place for anything but  compassion and concern during these  difficult times on april 12 2022 gilbert  godfrey passed away at the age of 67.  despite having only a few credits to his  name alex pettifer was on track to  become one of the first breakout stars  of the 2010s  his movie magic mic was one of the most  talked about films of the year earning  critical praise and making over 100  million dollars on a seven million  dollar budget however just before the  release of pedifer's i am number four  the hollywood reporter ran an expose  detailing the actor's misconduct on the  set of that film and on another upcoming  film beastly rather than do damage  control pettifer doubled down on the  animosity in an interview with v-man the  actor called los angeles a hole  continuing i think it's this insidious  pool where nearly everyone lives in fear  of his profession he likened acting to a  prison sentence quipping you go you  serve your time you try to replicate  johnny depp's career and then you move  to paris the actor later admitted that  the interview may had led to a rift with  his magic mike co-star channing tatum  whether or not the two still have beef  today pettifer wasn't invited back from  magic mike xxl and he's been relegated  to supporting roles in relatively  obscure projects ever since  clinton spillsbury only made two brief  tv appearances before securing the title  role in the big screen adventure the  legend of the lone ranger the reason  because he looked good in the  character's iconic mask producer martin  starger told entertainment weekly we had  to find an actor whose eyes were not  close together despite his  well-proportioned face spillsbury had no  experience with fame during the media  circuit leading up to the 1981 release  of the movie spillsbury agreed to a  meeting with andy warhol proprietor of  interview magazine in the andy warhol  diaries the famed artist wrote that the  actor had made some rather personal  admissions about his sexuality while  drunk spillsbury fell in love with  dennis christopher and then with that  kid bud court who was in herald and mod  then he said he'd been picked up by  fashion designer halston and woke up in  bed with him apart from that odd bit of  press spillsbury was apparently  difficult to work with the inexperienced  actor needed dialogue cuts because he  couldn't remember his lines to the point  that the producers eventually had to dub  him over with someone entirely different  the legend of the lone ranger flopped at  the box office earning 12.6 million  dollars and quickly disappearing from  theaters spillsbury disappeared too he'd  never act in another movie or tv series  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

